From: Alan Shearer
Subject: MediaPlayer: don't stop if nothing is loaded

Stop() and Pause() always talk to the playback manager. TogglePlaying
already checks InitCheck() first. These two didn't.

Open MediaPlayer with an empty playlist and press Esc. No file was
ever opened, so the node chain was never set up and _LastState() is
NULL. Stop() then seeks to 0 and crashes on that NULL.

Do the same InitCheck() test TogglePlaying uses. Still set fAutoplay.

#18714.

---
 src/apps/mediaplayer/Controller.cpp | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/apps/mediaplayer/Controller.cpp b/src/apps/mediaplayer/Controller.cpp
--- a/src/apps/mediaplayer/Controller.cpp
+++ b/src/apps/mediaplayer/Controller.cpp
@@ -626,8 +626,11 @@ Controller::Stop()
 
 	BAutolock _(this);
 
-	StopPlaying();
-	SetPosition(0.0);
+	if (InitCheck() == B_OK) {
+		StopPlaying();
+		SetPosition(0.0);
+	}
 
 	fAutoplay = fAutoplaySetting;
 }
@@ -653,7 +656,8 @@ Controller::Pause()
 
 	BAutolock _(this);
 
-	PausePlaying();
+	if (InitCheck() == B_OK)
+		PausePlaying();
 
 	fAutoplay = fAutoplaySetting;
 }
